      },
      "description": "The cluster centers on building and validating computational systems for complex signal-processing or hardware-oriented tasks, with a strong emphasis on implementation details rather than purely theoretical models. Most of the papers use formal design and simulation workflows—especially Verilog/HDL, HLS, FPGA synthesis, fault simulation, and protocol-level modeling—to turn specifications or extracted data into working hardware descriptions and to verify correctness and performance through testbenches, synthesis results, or simulation.\n\nA second thread is the use of data-driven automation for generation and analysis, either through multi-agent LLM pipelines for code creation/debugging or CNN-based models for recognition tasks such as deepfake detection and medical imaging. What ties them together is an engineering mindset focused on translating abstract input data into executable models or hardware/ML systems and then evaluating them with concrete, reproducible validation procedures."
